        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T01:46:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`apex_available` is not an authoritative factor that determines whether the module is included in the apex. The authoritative factor is the dependency type; In other words, the module will be included in the apex if it is a transitive/direct static dependency (i.e. `static_libs`) of an apex. However, `framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar` is only included as a dynamic dependency (i.e. `libs`) of modules included in the apex. This means that the module is not actually included in the apex. Thus, `apex_available` property set for `framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar` is a no-op from what I can tell. You would be able to observe that the build passes successfully even when you remove `apex_available` property from `framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar`.",
      "parentUuid": "107bb0f9_b7ea860a",
      "revId": "ce544f725b16ec51e849fabb333cbf55ee186d87",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
